INT. ARMORED PARKING GARAGE, P4 - NIGHT

Concrete. Sodium glare. Four people in a ring around a black sedan with its trunk open.

VIKTOR "VIC" ODUYA-LINDGREN (40s, tailored coat). ANNELIESE "ANNA" BRAITHWAITE-NKOSI (30s, gloves). REGINALD "REG" ASANTE-HOLM (50s, armed). And the fourth, tied to a chair, a gag around his neck: DEACON TIMOTHY ABARA-VOSS (60s, cufflinks).

VIC
Anna, take the gag off.

ANNA
Vic, he'll shout.

VIC
He won't.

REG
He will.

VIC
Deacon, will you shout?

DEACON
(hoarse)
No.

ANNA
He's lying.

VIC
He's tired. Tired men don't shout.

DEACON
Please, Victor.

VIC
Don't "please" me. You sold the list.

DEACON
I sold nothing.

REG
We've got the bank record.

DEACON
Then the bank record's wrong.

ANNA
Reg, check his phone.

REG
Already did. Nothing.

ANNA
Nothing doesn't mean innocent.

VIC
No. It means careful.

DEACON
Victor, listen. I wasn't the one.

VIC
Then who?

DEACON
(a long beat)
Ask her.

Every head turns toward Anna. She doesn't flinch.

ANNA
That's a nice try, Deacon.

DEACON
Check her laptop.

REG
Anna.

ANNA
Reg, don't.

VIC
Anna.

The ring tightens. In the silence, a distant door clanks open and footsteps echo down the ramp.
